g mechanism\"*, but merely because of the prompt's stipulated roles.\n    *   *Verification:* **VERIFIED_WITH_NON_MATERIAL_ISSUES**. Sections 6.1 and 6.2 define bare integers as *opaque structural identities* rather than informal numerals. Within the same inherited namespace (the enclosing subcase scope), the identical bare integer `1002` refers to the exact same object. Thus, the linkage is indeed a formally specified, native semantic mechanism (shared structural identity). This does not alter the validity of any conclusions regarding variable ownership or well-formedness.\n\n---\n\n### Verifier Disposition\n**VERIFIED_WITH_NON_MATERIAL_ISSUES**\n\n*   **Failed or Unresolved Obligations:** None. All structural outcomes, variable counts, ownership mappings, and well-formedness evaluations are correct. The only issue is a minor conceptual misclassification in the \"Difficulties\" commentary regarding bare integer namespace-sharing being described as informal \"numeral-matching.\"",
